# sy_codename_denylist.txt.example — TEMPLATE.
#
# Copy this file to sy_codename_denylist.txt (which is gitignored) and fill in
# YOUR tenant codenames and proper nouns. The real file never ships — your
# customer list is private (CLAUDE.md Rule 3: no tenant codename in the repo).
#
# One token per line. '#' and blank lines are ignored. Matching is substring +
# case-insensitive (see sy_scrub.scrub_codenames). Tokens are matched
# longest-first, so list snake_case variants explicitly (e.g. both 'acme_corp'
# and 'acmecorp'). Substring deliberately — '\b' would let 'acme_v2' slip past
# '\bacme\b'. Accept false positives over a real leak.
#
# The shipped placeholders below are NEUTRAL — replace every line.

# --- tenant codenames (replace with your own) ---
acme
acme_corp
acme_v2

# --- proper nouns (founder, brand, infra names that must not leak) ---
example_brand
